  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the reconsideration of how genomic language models segment sequence and handle context. MergeDNA replaces fixed tokenization with a differentiable token-merging tokenizer feeding latent Transformers, pre-trained via reconstruction, so segmentation is learned rather than prescribed. FOCUS addresses a complementary constraint: it is a plug-in progressive KV-cache compression module for pretrained DNA LLMs, reported to enable near-linear, roughly 100x longer inference with near-lossless behavior. The Evo2 study reports in-context learning in a genomic next-token predictor, with log-linear gains in pattern induction comparable to linguistic LLMs, extending that capability to genomic models. What is new is the joint attention to learned segmentation and long-context efficiency in DNA models. The items differ in method, so this thread describes the shared direction rather than a uniform approach across all three.",
